{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And they did so.</b> From where did they take the water? They brought it from another place, or alternatively from water that they dug. However, this is difficult for me, for after this it is written ״חפרו״, and in a single parashah it is not applicable to say 'there is no earlier and later in the Torah' unless forced by some other matter, as we explained above."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The word חפרו ('they dug') appears in the very next verse, Exodus 7:24, referring to the Egyptians digging around the Nile for water; the commentator notes the difficulty that the magicians would have needed water before that digging took place."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:49.633892238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}